The signed release store, archive validator, executable identity validation
and local selection state machine are new routerd2 code distributed under
the repository's BSD-3-Clause LICENSE.

No update-agent or bootloader implementation has been copied into this package.
It uses the Go standard library and golang.org/x/sys/unix through the project's
normal dependency graph. Their licenses, and the licenses of dependencies in
the released executable pair, remain part of the distribution materials.

The four-entry signed wire bundle does not embed license files. A distributor
must accompany the bundle with the project LICENSE and the dependency notices
and licenses for that exact build, as generated by the repository's packaging
license inventory. A successful signature check does not replace those
distribution materials.
